jessica_sales: Anne from DeltaSurge — demo stream is breaking for them, client sees JSON errors mid-stream.
anne_customer: yep — Android webview. logs attached to the ticket, here's an example payload where parser fails: '{\"id\":\"r1\",\"choices\":[{\"text\":\"incomple' (truncated)'.
paul_dev: we reproduced locally on Android webview, the parser gets "Unexpected end of input" when parsing a chunked event.
omar_se: can you upload a HAR or curl capture? need raw frames.
anne_customer: uploaded: https://files.example/deltasurge-har-04.zip
kate_e2e: I pulled the HAR — SSE lines are present but several events end without the blank-line terminator. looks like segments are split: 'data: {\"choices\": [\"par' then next frame 'tial...\"}]'
liam_infra: could be our runtime flush/optimizer or an edge proxy re-chunking. any internal proxies in front of the app?
paul_dev: yes, they run an internal edge proxy that does some buffering. no CDN.
omar_se: minimal reproduction suggests when the runtime experiences backpressure it may call socket.flush() between writes. that can leave an event block open across TCP frames. webview's JS parser tries to JSON.parse each arrival.
nick_support: short-term mitigations: 1) client-side buffer until you see the SSE event delimiter (\n\n) or a full JSON parse — cheapest. 2) ask infra to disable the optimizer/auto-flush. 3) provide Dedicated trial to avoid shared proxies.
liam_infra: checking commits — there was a change 2026-02-18 touching buffered writer that flips autoFlush after N tokens. rolling that back should close the window.
jessica_sales: timeline + cost for Dedicated? DeltaSurge is asking — they want reliable streams for live transcripts.
liam_infra: Dedicated onboarding typically 2-3 weeks; we can offer a short-term elevated quota (few days) while we patch. pricing on enterprise quote but we can do a trial.
omar_se: I'll prepare an SDK patch that buffers SSE fragments in the webview wrapper. low-risk and fast.
paul_dev: please provide a small snippet we can drop into our webview bridge.
omar_se: snippet below — it accumulates until full event separator and only then parses data: lines:
```js
let buf = '';
resp.addEventListener('data', chunk => {
  buf += chunk;
  let sepIdx;
  while ((sepIdx = buf.indexOf('\n\n')) !== -1) {
    const ev = buf.slice(0, sepIdx);
    buf = buf.slice(sepIdx + 2);
    const dataLines = ev.split('\n').filter(l => l.startsWith('data:'));
    const payload = dataLines.map(l => l.replace(/^data:\s*/, '')).join('\n');
    try {
      const parsed = JSON.parse(payload);
      handle(parsed);
    } catch (e) {
      // shouldn't happen if we buffer to separator; log for debugging
      console.warn('parse failed, keeping buffer', e);
      // re-buffer and break to wait for more data
      buf = ev + '\n\n' + buf;
      break;
    }
  }
});
```
liam_infra: I'll also instrument runtime with SSE_TRACE headers and logs: SSE_WRITE(id, len, flushed) to find early flush points.
deploy-bot: deploy queued: staging/runtime-rollback requested by @liam_infra — ETA 20m
nick_support: assign follow-ups: @omar_se SDK patch + PR, @liam_infra runtime revert + logs, @jessica_sales confirm Dedicated trial and pricing, customer to test client patch.
anne_customer: Paul will test the SDK change tomorrow morning PST. can you also send a prebuilt artifact if possible?
jessica_sales: we'll attach a trial key for elevated quota and send SOC/compliance overview in the same thread.
kate_e2e: I'll add an e2e that fuzzes fragment boundaries and ensures client-side reassemble works.
paul_dev: thanks, will try the snippet and report. if it passes, we can avoid infra rollback.
liam_infra: long-term fix: ensure producer always emits trailing blank line for SSE events and add unit tests for chunk boundaries. reverting the optimizer is low-risk.
nick_support: ETA estimates: SDK patch (PR + patch build) — same day; runtime rollback — ~1 day if rollback needs validation; Dedicated trial setup — 2-3 weeks for full onboarding but short-term quota within 24h.
jessica_sales: great, I'll keep the account exec and procurement loops updated. :thumbsup:
